# Release Engineering Workflow

Full policy: `docs/RELEASE_ENGINEERING_WORKFLOW.md`  
Hardening notes: `docs/releases/RELEASE-ENGINEERING-HARDENING.md`

## Source of truth

`main` and `origin/main` only. Feature branches are temporary.

## Canonical deploy entry

```bash
sudo bash deploy/manage_deploy.sh deploy full
```

One command owns the full normal-release pipeline (preflight → backup → migration decision → conditional schema-first → build → sync → post-sync migrate → restart → health → verify-release → smoke → report → SUCCESS).

Never deploy feature branches, dirty trees, or local-only commits.
Do not run standalone `migrate release` / `verify-release` / `smoke` as normal-release stages (diagnostics/recovery only).
Schema-first is auto-detected inside `deploy full`. Post-sync Alembic always runs (idempotent no-op OK).

## Lifecycle

Architecture Review → Implementation → Tests → Review → Fixes → Acceptance → Merge `main` → Validate → Push `origin/main` → Deploy (`deploy full`) → Product staging validation (separate)

## Hard rules

- Never merge or `git push origin main` without explicit user approval (ask separately).
- Never use `ALLOW_DIRTY_SYNC` / `DEPLOY_LOCAL_MAIN` / `--no-backup-db` for normal release deploys.
- Identity chain must match: origin/main == build-info == frontend identity == /api/build == tip APP_RELEASE.
- Release identity comes from tip `APP_RELEASE` (stale `RELEASE_VERSION` is warned and ignored).
- Restart and health failures are fatal (no soft-ignore).
- New deploy/release features go into `manage_deploy.sh` only (no new standalone deploy scripts except bootstrap/recovery).
